$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM tert-Butyl 5-(3-thienyl)thiophene-2-carboxylate (33). To a suspension of
Pd(PPh3)4 (0.18 g,0.16 mmol) in dry DME (20 mL) in an autoclave, compound
29 (1.36 g, 5.17 mmol) was added. The mixture was stirred for 10 min at
room temperature. 3-Thienylboronic acid (1.00 g, 7.81 mmol) and aqueous 2
M Na2CO3 solution (5.00 mL, 10.0 mmol) were added. The mixture was
stirred at 120 °C for 4 h. The solvent was evaporated under reduced
pressure, and the residue was suspended in H2O (50 mL). The aqueous
suspension was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 30 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with 10% KHSO4 (2 × 30 mL), H2O (30 mL), sat.
NaHCO3 (2 × 30 mL), H2O (30 mL) and brine (30 mL). The solvent was dried
(Na2SO4) and evaporated. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography using ethyl acetate/petroleum ether (1:30) to obtain 33.
Yellow oil,yield:0.99 g, 72%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 1.52 (s, 9H),
7.43 (d, 3J = 4.1 Hz, 1H), 7.49 (dd, 3J = 5.1 Hz, 4J = 1.0 Hz, 1H),
7.64-7.67 (m, 2H), 7.94 (dd, 3J = 2.9 Hz, 4J = 1.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR(125
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 27.98, 81.60, 122.67, 124.55, 126.12, 128.07, 132.27,
134.21, 134.25, 144.93, 160.79.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal (in stage 2), Suzuki coupling, autoclave used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective Nitrile Inhibitors To Modulate the Proteolytic Synergism of
Cathepsins S and F
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Frizler, Maxim; Schmitz, Janina; Schulz-Fincke, Anna-Christina;
Guetschow, Michael
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Medicinal Chemistry (2012), 55(12), 5982-5986

