$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
6-[6-(Methoxymethyl)-3-pyridinyl]-4-{[(1R)-1-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)ethyl]amino}-3-quinolinecarboxamide
(72). 2-(Methoxymethyl)-
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridine (86 mg, 0.34
mmol), tetrakis(triphenylphoshine)palladium (6.11 mg, 5 μmol), and cesium
carbonate (215 mg, 0.66 mmol) were added to a stirred suspension of
6-bromo-4-{[(1S)-1-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-
yl)ethyl]amino}-3-quinolinecarboxamide (100 mg, 0.26 mmol) in degassed
dioxane (2.2 mL) and water (0.25 mL) under nitrogen. The resulting
suspension was stirred at 80 °C for 2 h. The reaction mixture was then
allowed to cool to RT, concentrated, and the precipitate filtered and
washed with DCM. The filtrate was concentrated to dryness and purified by
preparative HPLC using decreasingly polar mixtures of water (containing
0.2% ammonium carbonate) and MeCN as eluent. The fractions were
evaporated to dryness.
7-Fluoro-6-[6-(methoxymethyl)-3-pyridinyl]-4-{[(1S)-1-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-
yl)ethyl]amino}-3-quinolinecarboxamide (73) The 7-fluoro analogue of 65
was prepared following the same procedure from 6-bromo-7-
fluoro-4-{[(1S)-1-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)ethyl]amino}-3-quinolinecarboxamide
(400 mg, 1.01 mmol).
7-Fluoro-6-[6-(methoxymethyl)-3-pyridinyl]-4-{[(1S)-1-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-
yl)ethyl]amino}-3-quinolinecarboxamide was obtained as a pale beige solid
(320 mg, 72%). 1H NMR (700 MHz, DMSO-d6, 303 K) 1.19-1.29 (5H, m), 1.52
(1H, d, J 12.2), 1.59 (1H, d, J 12.4), 1.72 (1H, dtt, J 3.4, 6.9, 11.5),
3.15-3.26 (2H, m), 3.41 (3H, s), 3.82 (2H, dt, J 4.5, 9.8), 3.90-3.99
(1H, m), 4.58 (2H, s), 7.48 (1H, s), 7.57 (1H, d, J 8.0), 7.66 (1H, d, J
11.9), 8.09 (2H, d, J 8.1), 8.37 (1H, d, J 8.3), 8.52 (1H, s), 8.65 (1H,
s), 8.80 (1H, s). 13C NMR (175 MHz, DMSO-d6, 300 K) 18.0, 28.8, 28.9,
41.6, 56.4, 58.1, 66.8, 66.9, 74.5, 109.2, 113.3 (d, J 20.8), 117.0,
120.9, 123.3 (d, J 16.9), 127.0, 129.4, 137.0, 148.6, 150.5 (d, J 12.7),
151.1, 152.4, 157.7, 159.1, 160.5, 170.7. HRMS (ESI+): Anal cald for
C24H28FN4O3 (M+H)+: 439.2145; Found: 439.2138.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
