$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure (i): Microwave assisted Suzuki coupling of
5-iodo-2-chloropyridine intermediates to boronic acids or esters. A
mixture of the 5-iodo-2-chloropyridine intermediate (1 eq.), appropriate
boronic acid or ester (1 eq.), Pd(PPh3)4 (5 mol%) and Na2CO3 (1.5 eq.) in
MeCN (7 mL mmol-1 of 5-iodo-2-chloropyridine intermediate) was heated at
100 °C in a microwave reactor for 30 min (for 4-aminopyridines) or 15 min
(for 4-methoxy and 4-thiomethylpyridines). The cooled reaction mixture
was absorbed onto silica gel and solvents were removed by evaporation.
Gradient silica column chromatography, eluting with 1-10% MeOH - CH2Cl2,
gave the coupled products.
2-Chloro-5-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-4-(methylthio)pyridine (52)
1-Methyl-4-(4,4,5,5- tetramethyl1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole was
reacted with 51 following General Procedure (i) to give 52 (72%) as a
yellow solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.11 (s, 1H), 7.69 (s, 1H), 7.63
(s, 1H), 7.04 (s, 1H), 3.95 (s, 3H), 2.46 (s, 3H); LC-MS (3.5 min) Rt =
2.53 min; m/z (ESI) 240 (M+H); HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd. for C10H11 35ClN3S
(M+H) 240.0357, found 240.0359.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, thermal, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 3-Alkoxyamino-5-(pyridin-2-ylamino)pyrazine-2-carbonitriles
as Selective, Orally Bioavailable CHK1 Inhibitors
