$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(5-Amino-pyridin-3-yl)-1-methyl-1H-indole (20). A flask was charged
with 3-amino-5-bromopyridine (4.05 g, 22.71 mmol),
N-methyl-indole-2-boronic acid (5.27 g, 29.52 mmol), s-Phos (0.625 g,
1.476 mmol), finely crushed potassium phosphate (9.74 g, 45.41 mmol), and
toluene (75 mL). After sparging with nitrogen for 60 min, Pd2dba3 (0.420
g, 0.454 mmol) was added, the flask was flushed with nitrogen, and the
flask was lowered into a preheated oil bath at 85 °C. After 1.5 h, the
mixture was allowed to cool to rt, diluted with ethyl acetate, and
filtered through a plug of silica gel (elution with ethyl acetate). The
residue was purified by silica gel flash chromatography (heptane-ethyl
acetate, 3:7 to 0:1). 20 (3.64 g, 16.30 mmol, 72%) as an off-white
powder. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ ppm 3.74 (s, 3 H), 5.49 (s, 2H),
6.56 (s, 1H), 7.05-7.09 (m, 1H), 7.09-7.10 (m, 1H), 7.17-7.21 (m, 1H),
7.49 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.57 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.94 (d, J = 2.0
Hz, 1 H), 7.99 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1 H). MS (ESI) m/z 224 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
N-[5-(6-Chloro-3-cyano-1-methyl-1H-indol-2-yl)-pyridin-3-ylmethyl]-ethanesulfonamide,
a Cortisol-Sparing CYP11B2 Inhibitor that Lowers Aldosterone in Human
Subjects
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
