$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Chloro-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide (12) Cesium carbonate
(14.4 g, 44.2 mmol) was added to 3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-
dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridine (3.74 g, 17.7 mmol),
6-bromo-4-chloroquinoline-3-carboxamide (5.1 g, 17.7 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphoshine)palladium (1.0 g, 0.9 mmol) in dioxane (45 mL)
and water (6.4 mL) at 20 °C under nitrogen. The resulting slurry was
stirred at 100 °C for 5 hours and allowed to cool to RT. Water (150 mL)
was then added and the solid was filtered, washed with water (2 x 100 mL)
and MeCN (3 x 80 mL) and dried at 50 °C under vacuum.
4-chloro-6-(pyridin-3-yl)quinoline-3-carboxamide (3.60 g, 72%) as a
bright yellow solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6, 300 K) 7.55-7.63 (1H, m),
7.97 (1H, s), 8.17-8.34 (4H, m), 8.53 (1H, d), 8.68 (1H, dd), 8.91 (1H,
s), 9.10 (1H, d). m/z 284.4 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key intermediate, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Novel 3-Quinoline Carboxamides as Potent, Selective, and
Orally Bioavailable Inhibitors of Ataxia Telangiectasia Mutated (ATM)
Kinase
