$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
7-Phenyl-1-(4-methoxybenzenesulfonyl)-6-azaindole (12). A mixture of 28
(0.10 g, 0.27 mmol) in toluene (8 mL),
tetrakis-(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0.02 g, 0.02 mmol), 2 M of K2CO3
(1 mL), phenylboronic acid (0.04 g, 0.3 mmol), and EtOH (5 mL) was heated
to reflux under N2 for 24 h. The solvent was then removed under reduced
pressure and the resulting residue was purified with flash chromatography
(2:3 EtOAc/n-hexane).
7-(2-Furanyl)-1-(4-methoxybenzenesulfonyl)-6-azaindole (21). The title
compound was obtained in 72% overall yield from compound 28 in a manner
similar to that described for the preparation of 12 as a solid. mp
136.3-137.8 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.79 (s, 3H), 6.56 (m, 1H),
6.70 (d, J = 3.70 Hz, 1H), 6.80 (d, J = 8.94 Hz, 2H), 6.83 (d, J = 3.31
Hz, 1H), 7.36 (d, J = 5.14 Hz, 1H), 7.42 (d, J = 9.02 Hz, 2H), 7.74 (d, J
= 3.71 Hz, 1H), 8.43 (d, J = 5.08 Hz, 1H); MS (ESI) m/z 377.0 (M + Na);
HRMS (ESI) for C18H15N2O4S (M + H+) calcd, 355.0753; found, 355.0763.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling, literature procedure
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Furanylazaindoles: Potent Anticancer Agents in Vitro and in Vivo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
