$DATUM 14c: A mixture of compound 11 (625mg, 2.2equiv), compound 13 (150mg,
1equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (24mg,10%equiv), K2CO3 (140mg, 5equiv) in 50 ml THF (2
ml H2O) was stirred at 66°C for 18 h under nitrogen. After cooling to
room temperature, the reaction mixture was poured into water and the
product was extracted with diethyl ether. The solvent was evaporated
under reduced pressure, and the crude product was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/CH2Cl2, 4:1) to yield the
yellow waxy product (456mg, 72%). 14c. Yield 456mg, 72%. 1H NMR (CDCl3,
400 MHz, 298K): δ = 8.82-8.76 (m, 8H), 8.68 (s, 4H), 8.10 (m, 6H),
7.88-7.84 (m, 8H), 7.72 (t, 4H), 4.71 (s, 6H), 4.35 (d, 8H), 2.4 (s, 3H),
1.85 (s, 4H), 1.46-1.11 (m, 232H), 0.89-0.72 (m, 42H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
150 MHz, 298K): δ = 166.3, 143.1, 137.3, 136.7, 135.7, 135.3, 132.9,
132.6, 132.3, 131.6, 131.2, 130.9, 130.7, 129.7, 129.4, 127.7, 125.2,
125.1, 125.0, 124.9, 123.6, 121.3, 117.9, 117.5, 117.2, 115.9, 114.9,
68.4, 50.6, 40.2, 37.7, 32.6, 32.1, 31.7, 30.2, 29.9, 29.6, 29.4, 27.0,
26.7, 22.9, 22.8, 14.6, 14.0. MS (MALDI-TOF): m/z (M+) =3140.0 (calcd for
C220H325N3O8: 3140.1).
