$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
compounds 53–55. To 52 (1 equiv.), boronic acid (8 equiv.), Pd(PPh3)4 (12
mol%), NaOH (6 equiv., 1.5 M), toluene (5 mL) and EtOH (0.5 mL) were
added and the reaction mixture was stirred at 90 °C overnight. EtOAc (30
mL) was added to the reaction mixture and the organic phase was washed
with water, dried and concentrated under vacuum. The crude products were
purified on column chromatography to obtain the products 53–55.
3-[3-(2-Phenylimidazol-1-ylmethyl)phenyl]-5-isobutylthiophene-2-(N-tert-butyl)sulfonamide
(53). The compound 53 was synthesized from 52 (75.5 mg, 148 μmol)
following the general procedure using phenylboronic acid (144 mg, 1.18
mmol). The crude product was purified (EtOAc:hexan 80:20)
3-[3-(2-Thiophen-3-yl-imidazol-1-ylmethyl)phenyl]-5-isobutylthiophene-2-(N-tert-butyl)sulfonamide
(54). The compound 54 was synthesized from 52 (61.7 mg, 121 μmol)
following the general procedure using 3-thienylboronic acid (124 mg,
0.968 mmol). The crude product was purified (EtOAc:hexan 80:20 to 90:10).
3-[3-(2-Thiophen-3-yl-imidazol-1-ylmethyl)phenyl]-5-isobutylthiophene-2-(N-tert-butyl)sulfonamide
54 (44.3 mg, 86.2 μmol, 72%) 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ: 0.95(d, J = 6.4 Hz, 6H),
0.96 (s, 9H), 1.82-2.00 (m, 1H), 2.65 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 4.08 (br s,
1H), 5.32 (s, 2H), 6.69 (s, 1H), 6.97 (s, 1H), 7.05 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H),
7.16 (s, 1H), 7.30-7.46 (m, 5H), 7.52 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ: 22.1, 29.5, 30.5, 39.1, 50.2, 54.6, 121.2, 124.1, 126.1,
126.4, 127.3, 127.9, 128.6, 128.8, 128.9, 129.1, 131.1, 135.7, 136.6,
137.0, 142.4, 143.9, 148.6; IR (cm-1) ν: 3276, 3107, 2960, 2869, 1464,
1439, 1388, 1315; Anal. Calcd for (C26H31N3O2S3) C, 60.8; H, 6.1; N, 8.2.
Found: C, 60.4; H, 6.0; N, 8.0.
