$DATUM 4,7-Di(pyridin-2-yl)benzo[c][1,2,5]thiadiazole[7] (15) A degassed
suspension of 14 (2.18 g, 5.62 mmol), 2-bromopyridine (1.0 mL, 11 mmol),
K2CO3 (4.66 g, 33.7 mmol), and [Pd(PPh3)4] (0.33 g, 0.28 mmol) in toluene
(20 mL) and H2O (5 mL) was heated for 48 h at 80 °C. The mixture was
extracted with Et2O, and the organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, filtered, and the solvent was evaporated. FC (SiO2;
cyclohexane/EtOAc 8:2 → 1:1) afforded 15. Yield (1.16 g, 71 %). Rf = 0.35
(SiO2; cyclohexane/EtOAc 1:1); m.p. 131 - 133 °C ([7]: 145 - 147 °C); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.40 (ddd, J = 7.5, 4.8, 1.1, 2H), 7.94 (td, J
= 7.8, 1.9, 2H), 8.63 (s, 2H), 8.73 (dt, J = 7.9, 1.1, 2H), 8.85 ppm
(ddd, J = 4.8, 1.8, 0.9, 2H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 123.16,
125.16, 129.67, 132.36, 136.63, 149.83, 153.80, 154.09 ppm; IR (ATR): ν-
= 3412 (w), 3046 (w), 2991 (w), 1989 (w), 1904 (w), 1730 (w), 1580 (m),
1568 (m), 1546 (m), 1498 (w), 1459 (m), 1437 (m), 1429 (m), 1369 (m),
1347 (m), 1294 (m), 1261 (w), 1241 (w), 1154 (m), 1132 (w), 1053 (m), 993
(m), 948 (m), 889 (m), 858 (s), 840 (m), 805 (m), 770 (s), 735 (s), 727
(s), 660 (m), 637 (m), 618 cm−1 (m); HR-MALDI-MS (3-HPA): m/z (%):
291.0699 (100, [M+H]+, calcd for C16H11N4S+: 291.0660).
