$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-Substituted-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydroisoquinolin-1(2H)-one
(I-34). To a 50 mL roundbottomed flask under an atmosphere of nitrogen
was added 4,4,4,4',5,5,5',5'-octamethy2,2'-bi(1,3,2-dioxaborolane) (0.401
g, 1.578 mmol), intermediate I-33 (1.435 mmol), and potassium acetate
(0.422 g, 4.30 mmol) in 25 mL of DMSO to give an orange solution.
Pdcl2(dppf)-CH2Cl2 adduct (0.070 g, 0.086 mmol) was added. The reaction
was heated to 80 °C and allowed to stir for 16 h. The mixture was then
poured into 100 mL of water and extracted with three 50 mL portions of
ethyl acetate. The combined organic layers were washed with water and
brine, dried overmagnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. The
residue was purified by silica gel to give the desired product.
2-Benzy4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydroisoquinolin-1(2H)-one
(I-34−4). General procedure G was followed to give I-34−4 from I-33−4,
71% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CHLOROFORM-d) δ 1.28 (s, 12 H) 1.62 -1.80 (m,
4 H) 2.46 - 2.60 (m, 2 H) 2.73 - 2.85 (m, 2 H) 5.12 (s, 2 H) 7.21 - 7.36
(m, 5 H) 7.67 (s, 1 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
