$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 4,5-bis(2,5-dimethylthien-3-yl)-thiophene-2-carboxylate
(3ThCOOMe). To a solution mixture of methyl
4,5-dibromothiophene-2-carboxylate (2 mmol), 2,5-dimethylthien-3-yl
boronic acid (1.87 g, 12 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (321 mg, 0.36 mmol) in THF (200
mL) was added aqueous sodium carbonate solution (2 M, 1.7 g, 8 mL, 16
mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred and heated to reflux in the dark.
The progress was monitored by TLC. This was then extracted with
chloroform, washed with brine, and finally dried over anhydrous magnesium
sulfate. After filtration and removal of the solvent, the crude product
was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (70-230 mesh) using
n-hexane-dichloromethane (4:1 v/v) as the eluent. Further purification
was achieved by recrystallization from hot hexane-dichloromethane to give
the product as a white solid. Yield: 71 %. Methyl
4,5-bis(2,5-dimethylthien-3-yl)-thiophene-2-carboxylate (3ThCOOMe).
Yield: 71 %. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K, relative to Me4Si): δ 2.03
(s, 3H, Me), 2.05 (s, 3H, Me), 2.36 (s, 6H, Me), 3.89 (s, 3H, COOMe),
6.39 (s, 1H, thienyl-H), 6.46 (s, 1H, thienyl-H), 7.71 (s, 1H,
thienyl-H). 13C NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K, relative to Me4Si): δ
13.73, 13.93, 15.06, 15.12, 52.15, 126.83, 127.20, 129.74, 130.59,
132.23, 133.38, 135.07, 135.39, 135.59, 135.87, 135.94, 141.25, 162.77.
Positive FAB-MS: m/z 362 {M}+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Versatile Photochromic Dithienylethene-Containing β-Diketonate Ligand:
Near-Infrared Photochromic Behavior and Photoswitchable Luminescence
Properties upon Incorporation of a Boron(III) Center
