$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura Cross-coupling. A literature
procedure was used. 15 To a 4-dram vial was added the appropriate
iodoheterocycle (0.125 mmol), the boronic acid (1.4 equiv, 0.175 mmol),
KHCO3 (1.4 equiv, 0.175 mmol) and PdCl2 (5 mol %) in 4:1 DMF:H2O (2.5
mL). The solution was stirred for 5 min at room temperature and flushed
with Ar and then heated to 80°C for 2 h. After cooling, the reaction
mixture was diluted with EtOAc, washed with satd aq NH4Cl, brine and
water. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under
vacuum to give the crude product, which was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel using hexane-EtOAc as the eluent.
6-[2-(2-Phenylbenzofuran-3-yl)benzo[b]thiophen-3-yl]-1H-indole (35). The
product was obtained (yield = 71%) as a brown solid 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 6.37 (s, 1H), 7.04-7.06 (m, 2H), 7.12 (t, J= 8.0 Hz, 2H),
7.19-7.25 (m, 4H), 7.34-7.45 (m, 4H), 7.50 (s, 1H), 7.67-7.68 (m, 2H),
7.81 (d, J= 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (d, J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.96 (br s, 1H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 103.07, 103.12, 110.5, 110.9, 111.1, 120.6, 121.9,
122.6, 123.2, 124.1, 124.4, 124.7, 124.8, 126.5, 127.0, 127.9, 128.6,
128.7, 129.1, 130.4, 130.8, 135.2, 138.2, 140.6, 140.8, 153.1, 153.9 (one
signal missing due to overlap); HRMS Calcd for C30H19NOS: 441.11873.
Found: 441.12003.
